WEBVTT

00:00.728 --> 00:03.596
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.166 --> 00:07.435
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.469 --> 00:11.005
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.039 --> 00:14.008
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.042 --> 00:17.511
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:17.546 --> 00:20.815
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.849 --> 00:22.383
♪ All the things that make us

00:22.417 --> 00:23.751
♪ Laugh and cry

00:23.785 --> 00:25.301
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.329 --> 00:37.698
<i>ANNOUNCER (over TV):We now return to
Home Alone with Competent Robbers.</i>

00:43.205 --> 00:45.106
Hey, be careful. There's
cars on the floor here.

00:45.140 --> 00:46.907
Thanks.
That's weird, huh?

00:46.942 --> 00:48.476
Yeah. The doorknob
was really hot,

00:48.510 --> 00:50.911
but I just let go instead
of holding onto it.

00:50.946 --> 00:53.180
And there's some ice
on the stairs to the basement,

00:53.215 --> 00:55.716
so I guess just
don't go down there.

00:55.751 --> 00:57.985
Just so you guys know,
I have a tarantula.

01:00.389 --> 01:02.323
Well, now there
are no witnesses.

01:02.357 --> 01:04.825
Come on, everybody,
let's go to the mall.

01:04.860 --> 01:06.894
It's time for the
Christmas Carnival.

01:06.928 --> 01:09.163
It's Stewie's
first Christmas.

01:09.197 --> 01:10.364
Again?

01:10.399 --> 01:13.401
I love the
Christmas Carnival!

01:13.435 --> 01:14.568
Chris, calm down.

01:14.603 --> 01:16.237
You're giving
yourself a nosebleed.

01:16.271 --> 01:18.105
You know, the best thing
about the Quahog Mall

01:18.140 --> 01:20.708
is going into Tiffany's
and doing everything possible

01:20.742 --> 01:23.010
to make 'em think I might
actually buy something.

01:23.044 --> 01:25.379
Oh, this is lovely.
Just lovely.

01:25.414 --> 01:26.547
How much is this?

01:26.581 --> 01:27.982
$1,200.

01:28.016 --> 01:29.283
Great, great.

01:29.317 --> 01:31.585
That's all? A-And how late
are you open this evening?

01:31.620 --> 01:32.586
Until 7:00.

01:32.621 --> 01:33.654
Perfect, perfect.

01:33.688 --> 01:35.517
And you accept
credit cards and cash?

01:35.518 --> 01:36.266
Yes.

01:36.267 --> 01:37.092
And what's your name?

01:37.097 --> 01:39.331
I want to make sure you
get credit for this sale.

01:39.361 --> 01:41.495
Evan.
Oh, that's a great name.

01:41.530 --> 01:42.930
Oh, and these watches here,

01:42.964 --> 01:45.399
if I wanted to get 11 of them
for different groomsmen,

01:45.434 --> 01:47.416
could they each get
engraved individually?

01:47.441 --> 01:48.169
Yes.

01:48.170 --> 01:49.870
And you do that on site?
Yes.

01:49.905 --> 01:53.908
Fantastic. Now, the groomsmen's
names are Blake, Hayden, Edgar,

01:53.942 --> 01:57.278
Blake D., Elliott,
Milo, Cooper...

01:57.312 --> 01:58.946
Why aren't you writing
any of these down?

01:58.980 --> 02:01.549
You're wearing Sbarro
wrappers for shoes, sir.

02:03.151 --> 02:05.219
<i>There may have been
a trade.</i>

02:12.861 --> 02:14.929
Hey, nice outfit.

02:14.963 --> 02:17.198
Fancy pair of shoes, too.

02:17.232 --> 02:20.034
Do you, do you only use
adjectives sarcastically?

02:20.068 --> 02:23.170
Great question,
smart guy.

02:23.205 --> 02:25.039
What the hell?
Where's all the decorations?

02:25.073 --> 02:26.373
And the big Christmas tree?

02:26.408 --> 02:27.408
Oh, look, there's Santa.

02:27.442 --> 02:28.576
Peter, no.

02:28.610 --> 02:30.077
That's a Hells Angel.

02:30.111 --> 02:31.078
What do you want?

02:31.112 --> 02:31.979
Meth?

02:32.013 --> 02:33.013
Okay.

02:33.048 --> 02:35.182
There's no
Christmas Carnival, Dad.

02:35.217 --> 02:36.684
You seem to know
a lot about this, Meg.

02:36.718 --> 02:37.651
What did you do?

02:37.686 --> 02:39.487
No Christmas Carnival?

02:39.521 --> 02:40.921
Whoever is responsible
for this

02:40.956 --> 02:42.556
shall suffer
my eternal wrath.

02:42.591 --> 02:44.258
(chuckles)
Who's this guy?

02:44.292 --> 02:45.759
Tough don't sell
in curly-toed shoes.

02:45.794 --> 02:47.294
Leave me alone.

02:47.329 --> 02:50.164
Why don't you go bother
the cologne salesman at Macy's?

02:50.198 --> 02:51.866
I want something I
can wear on the street

02:51.900 --> 02:54.602
that a broad can smell
on a fire escape.

02:54.636 --> 02:56.904
There's gotta be
an explanation for this.

02:56.938 --> 02:58.205
Let's ask that security guard

02:58.240 --> 03:00.207
who has everything on
his belt except a gun.

03:00.242 --> 03:02.142
E-Excuse me, sir?

03:02.177 --> 03:03.244
It's "officer."

03:03.278 --> 03:05.513
No, it's not.
It's barely "sir."

03:05.547 --> 03:06.680
Yeah, I know.

03:06.715 --> 03:08.716
Where is
the Christmas Carnival?

03:08.750 --> 03:10.384
Canceled.
I don't know why.

03:10.418 --> 03:12.686
I'm just a small cog
in this operation.

03:12.721 --> 03:13.988
You hear that, Dad?

03:14.022 --> 03:16.624
You're not the only one
around here with a small cog.

03:16.658 --> 03:19.460
PETER and LOIS: I told you that
in confidence, Chris.

03:19.494 --> 03:21.428
Daddy, where's Santa?

03:21.463 --> 03:23.330
Was he killed by Muslims?

03:23.365 --> 03:25.266
Oh, my God,
poor Stewie.

03:25.300 --> 03:27.101
He's so
disappointed.

03:27.135 --> 03:29.270
Of course he is, Lois.
I feel the same way.

03:29.304 --> 03:31.071
How come every time
I'm feelin' happy,

03:31.106 --> 03:32.940
somebody's gotta
come along and ruin it?

03:34.175 --> 03:35.676
Are you enjoying
your coffee, sir?

03:35.710 --> 03:37.611
Yeah, it's very
smooth. Good flavor.

03:37.646 --> 03:40.814
What if we told you that
we secretly replaced your coffee

03:40.849 --> 03:42.116
with Folgers Crystals?

03:42.150 --> 03:43.651
Wouldn't you
feel like a dumbass?

03:43.685 --> 03:45.719
'Cause of how you just
raved about it just now?

03:45.754 --> 03:47.788
You stupid
son of a bitch.

03:54.930 --> 03:56.430
Boy, Stewie was
really upset

03:56.464 --> 03:58.732
about the Christmas
Carnival being canceled.

03:58.767 --> 04:00.067
He's been acting
out all week.

04:00.101 --> 04:02.269
Ah, I'm sure he'll
be over it in no time.

04:02.304 --> 04:04.738
Besides, how much trouble
can he cause? He's a baby.

04:08.977 --> 04:10.177
(hisses)

04:15.116 --> 04:18.986
<i>ANNOUNCER (over TV): We now return to
Miracle on 134th Street.</i>

04:19.020 --> 04:21.822
Oh, my God, I left
my phone in my car.

04:21.856 --> 04:24.425
Wow, it's still there.

04:29.698 --> 04:33.100
Hey, I've been askin' around
about this carnival thing.

04:33.134 --> 04:35.135
Turns out I know a guy
who knows a guy

04:35.170 --> 04:37.104
who knows another guy
who knows a girl,

04:37.138 --> 04:39.573
which is weird because they
don't usually know nothin',

04:39.608 --> 04:42.076
who says the carnival was
canceled by the mall's owner,

04:42.110 --> 04:43.711
some guy named
Carter Pewterschmidt.

04:43.745 --> 04:45.112
Oh, my God.

04:45.146 --> 04:48.048
So I got another guy workin'
on findin' out who that is.

04:48.083 --> 04:49.283
It's my father.

04:49.317 --> 04:52.252
Oh! This is a twist
I did not expect.

04:52.287 --> 04:55.489
Oh! Excuse me, I'm just gonna
have to "Oh" this out

04:55.523 --> 04:57.491
until I'm not
surprised anymore.

04:57.525 --> 05:00.027
Oh! Oh! Oh.

05:00.061 --> 05:03.297
Oh... Oh. Oh.

05:03.331 --> 05:05.099
Lois, before I get mad
at your dad,

05:05.133 --> 05:06.900
h-he isn't the Little
Caesars guy, is he?

05:06.935 --> 05:08.296
No, Peter,
we've been through this.

05:08.303 --> 05:10.270
Good. I could never
be mad at that guy.

05:10.305 --> 05:12.239
He says my favorite word
twice in a row.

05:12.273 --> 05:13.941
Now, I'm gonna go
talk to your father

05:13.975 --> 05:15.909
and get him to bring back
the Christmas Carnival.

05:15.944 --> 05:17.478
Peter, I don't think
that's gonna work.

05:17.512 --> 05:18.946
Sure, it will.

05:18.980 --> 05:21.215
The nerve of your dad, takin'
the fun out of Christmas,

05:21.249 --> 05:23.384
like some kind of
gluten-free Santa.

05:24.352 --> 05:25.853
Hey. Hey,
what's in these?

05:25.887 --> 05:27.021
Huh?

05:27.055 --> 05:29.189
I'm okay if it's,
like, coconut flour.

05:29.224 --> 05:31.792
But anything with actual
grains, I can't do.

05:31.826 --> 05:33.060
I'm not sure.

05:33.094 --> 05:35.429
<i>Well, who is sure?</i>

05:39.734 --> 05:41.235
(squeaking)

05:46.074 --> 05:47.574
WOMAN: Mr. Pewterschmidt,
there's a man here

05:47.609 --> 05:50.244
who says he's the guy whose
picture is on all the money.

05:50.278 --> 05:51.779
Holy cow. Send him in.

05:53.014 --> 05:54.548
Griffin.

05:54.582 --> 05:57.151
<i>That's right, and this is my
own People magazine from home</i>

05:57.185 --> 05:58.819
and not from your
waiting room just now,

05:58.853 --> 06:00.721
and why did you cancel
the Christmas Carnival?

06:00.755 --> 06:02.189
Because I hate Christmas.

06:02.223 --> 06:04.525
You know what it's like being
rich at Christmas, Griffin?

06:04.559 --> 06:07.995
Everyone expects an expensive
present, and I get nothing.

06:08.029 --> 06:10.798
Did you... did you just have
your hand in my fish tank?

06:10.832 --> 06:12.066
No.

06:12.100 --> 06:13.260
Sheesh, Carter,
you know what?

06:13.268 --> 06:15.402
I am gonna help you find
the Christmas spirit

06:15.437 --> 06:16.770
so you bring back
the carnival.

06:16.805 --> 06:17.938
Look, are we done here?

06:17.972 --> 06:19.473
Um, yeah, uh, just
one more thing.

06:19.507 --> 06:22.276
Can I choose one thing in your office
to take home with me?

06:22.310 --> 06:23.544
No.

06:23.578 --> 06:27.214
Aw, too bad. 'Cause I
was gonna choose you.

06:27.248 --> 06:29.650
You're weird.
You're a weird guy.

06:34.598 --> 06:36.899
No. No-no, no.

06:36.933 --> 06:38.100
I want to zip it.

06:40.103 --> 06:41.704
(grunts)

06:41.738 --> 06:44.240
It's okay, Peter,
you're good at other stuff.

06:44.274 --> 06:45.775
So you're gonna
help your old man

06:45.809 --> 06:47.643
find his Christmas
spirit again, huh?

06:47.678 --> 06:49.445
Oh, yeah, that
sounds real bad,

06:49.479 --> 06:51.380
her father don't
like Christmas.

06:51.415 --> 06:53.549
My father was drowned
to death in a birdbath

06:53.583 --> 06:55.284
by an officer
of the law.

06:55.319 --> 06:56.419
His will just said,

06:56.453 --> 06:58.788
"Kick Jimmy in the sack
for me. Go, Eagles."

06:58.822 --> 07:00.222
My sympathies, Vinny.

07:00.257 --> 07:02.458
Don't worry about it,
he was a scumbag.

07:02.492 --> 07:04.093
Are you sure
about this, Peter?

07:04.127 --> 07:06.162
I mean, I know
Stewie was disappointed

07:06.196 --> 07:08.064
about the carnival,
but he'll get over it.

07:08.098 --> 07:09.765
He's a happy,
resilient baby.

07:09.800 --> 07:11.033
I don't know, Lois.

07:11.068 --> 07:12.668
I feel like if we
don't do something,

07:12.703 --> 07:14.024
Stewie's first
words are gonna be,

07:14.037 --> 07:15.371
"Why did you
kill Christmas?"

07:15.405 --> 07:16.939
And I want the
carnival back, too.

07:16.973 --> 07:19.408
You know, I know I'm usually
all business, but deep down,

07:19.443 --> 07:21.610
you know what the thing
is that keeps me going

07:21.645 --> 07:22.645
more than
anything else?

07:22.679 --> 07:23.946
Wonder.

07:23.980 --> 07:25.915
A sense of wonder.

07:25.949 --> 07:28.184
Well, you have your work
cut out for you, Peter.

07:28.218 --> 07:31.053
My father's always
hated Christmas.

07:31.088 --> 07:33.222
Hey, happy June 16.

07:33.256 --> 07:35.291
Thought I'd see how
you like it when someone

07:35.325 --> 07:37.893
breaks into your house
and touches all your stuff.

07:37.928 --> 07:39.395
Hey. Knock it off.

07:39.429 --> 07:41.330
I'm touching this.
And this over here.

07:41.365 --> 07:43.432
You're a creep,
is my point.

07:46.470 --> 07:48.037
All right, Carter, now,
you know what's guaranteed

07:48.071 --> 07:49.472
to put you
in the holiday mood?

07:49.506 --> 07:50.539
Write a Christmas letter

07:50.574 --> 07:52.208
to all your friends
and relatives.

07:52.242 --> 07:54.343
And keep in mind,
it's traditional to embellish

07:54.378 --> 07:56.112
a little bit to make
yourself look better.

07:56.146 --> 07:57.580
"Peter had a
great year,

07:57.614 --> 07:59.248
"and is now starting
quarterback

07:59.282 --> 08:01.283
for the Jacksonville
Jaguars."

08:01.318 --> 08:03.552
What? People can easily
fact-check this.

08:03.587 --> 08:05.354
Yeah, who has the time?
Keep reading.

08:05.389 --> 08:07.490
"Chris refurbished a
vintage motorcycle,

08:07.524 --> 08:09.291
"and Stewie can
slam-dunk a basketball

08:09.326 --> 08:10.993
from a standing
start..."

08:11.027 --> 08:12.328
Peter, that's
impossible.

08:12.362 --> 08:13.763
Read what it says
about you.

08:13.797 --> 08:15.698
"Lois's father,
Carter Pewterschmidt,

08:15.732 --> 08:17.500
bought a small stool
for his balls."

08:17.534 --> 08:18.934
Damn it, I'm not
proud of that.

08:18.969 --> 08:20.870
Well, you have to
throw in some real facts.

08:20.904 --> 08:23.272
That's what gives
the newsletter credibility.

08:25.041 --> 08:27.676
Now, everyone knows the best way
to get the Christmas spirit

08:27.711 --> 08:30.613
is to drink a whole lot
of thick, frothy eggnog.

08:30.647 --> 08:31.447
So get going.

08:31.481 --> 08:32.481
I don't like eggnog.

08:32.516 --> 08:33.549
Drink the nog, Carter.

08:33.583 --> 08:35.017
I don't... I don't want to.

08:35.051 --> 08:37.420
Take it, Carter.
Take all the nog.

08:37.454 --> 08:39.989
(coughs)

08:40.023 --> 08:41.157
No.

08:41.191 --> 08:42.525
Yeah, you like that nog.

08:42.559 --> 08:43.893
Don't spit
the nog out.

08:43.927 --> 08:45.995
Now look at the
camera for a POV shot.

08:46.029 --> 08:48.164
Say thank you with
the nog in your mouth.

08:48.198 --> 08:49.265
Thank you.
Louder.

08:49.299 --> 08:50.699
Thank you.

08:50.734 --> 08:53.068
Good, now go down
to the hotel lobby and check out

08:53.103 --> 08:54.336
with nog all
over your face.

08:54.371 --> 08:55.404
All right.

08:55.439 --> 08:57.373
You know, I still
don't like Christmas,

08:57.407 --> 08:59.675
but I kind of like
what we just did.

09:01.445 --> 09:04.280
Okay, Carter, a big part
of Christmas is masturbating

09:04.314 --> 09:06.615
like you would any other day
but feeling guilty about it

09:06.650 --> 09:08.284
because it's Christmas.

09:13.957 --> 09:16.392
(sighs) What's
wrong with me?

09:16.426 --> 09:17.393
Griffin,
this isn't working.

09:17.427 --> 09:18.594
What? What do you mean?

09:18.628 --> 09:20.162
I-I'm not getting
the holiday spirit,

09:20.197 --> 09:21.330
so you can stop trying.

09:21.364 --> 09:22.865
But Carter, it's
not just for me.

09:22.899 --> 09:24.200
Think about Stewie.

09:24.234 --> 09:26.068
He's all upset 'cause
there's no carnival.

09:26.102 --> 09:27.470
Heh.
Different dog.

09:27.504 --> 09:29.405
Yeah, this one's, like,
Italian or something.

09:29.439 --> 09:30.806
Anyway, I think
we're done here.

09:30.841 --> 09:32.274
No Christmas Carnival.

09:32.309 --> 09:34.743
Wow, Carter. I had no
idea you were Jewish.

09:34.778 --> 09:36.979
What? Is... is that
how this is coming off?

09:37.013 --> 09:38.247
Yeah, kind of.

09:38.281 --> 09:39.648
I mean, that's what
everyone's saying.

09:39.683 --> 09:41.317
People think I'm Jewish?

09:52.629 --> 09:56.031
Oh, this Christmas Carnival
has everything. Games, food.

09:56.066 --> 09:58.634
<i>Oh, my God, it's the carolers
from A Christmas Story.</i>

09:58.668 --> 10:02.471
♪ Deck the harrs
with boughs of horry ♪

10:02.506 --> 10:06.141
♪ Fa ra ra ra ra
ra ra ra ra ♪

10:06.176 --> 10:07.977
That's right, America,
don't forget.

10:08.011 --> 10:10.913
Your beloved holiday movie
is incredibly racist.

10:10.947 --> 10:12.982
And flom
not that rong ago.

10:13.049 --> 10:14.650
What's wrong with you,
Stews?

10:14.684 --> 10:16.585
You're next up
to see the big guy himself

10:16.620 --> 10:19.021
and you look like a piece
of spaghetti on the street.

10:19.055 --> 10:21.023
I don't know. I thought
having the carnival back

10:21.057 --> 10:22.258
would make me happy,

10:22.292 --> 10:24.360
but it still feels like
something's missing.

10:24.394 --> 10:26.161
Yeah, it's always somethin'.

10:26.196 --> 10:28.464
Like when I finally got
to sleep with Mary Lou Gallo.

10:28.498 --> 10:30.766
She had a look,
but when you got up close,

10:30.800 --> 10:32.635
she also had a smell.

10:32.669 --> 10:34.637
Oh, Stewie, you're next.

10:34.671 --> 10:36.605
Ho ho ho.

10:36.640 --> 10:38.140
Mall Santa is
brought to you

10:38.174 --> 10:40.309
in part this season
by Chipotle.

10:40.343 --> 10:43.178
Between good and
garbage, it's Chipotle.

10:43.213 --> 10:45.114
So, what do you want
for Christmas?

10:45.148 --> 10:47.049
Oh, what do I want
for Christmas?

10:47.083 --> 10:49.351
<i>What do I want
for Christmas?</i>

10:56.359 --> 10:58.227
You know what I want
for Christmas?

10:58.261 --> 11:00.095
I want my friend back.

11:00.130 --> 11:01.330
Your friend?

11:01.364 --> 11:02.765
Yes. My best friend.

11:02.799 --> 11:04.600
My dog, Brian.

11:04.634 --> 11:06.235
He's dead.

11:06.269 --> 11:08.404
It's our first Christmas
without him

11:08.438 --> 11:11.140
and no one's even
mentioned his name.

11:13.176 --> 11:15.878
I don't care about this stupid
carnival or Christmas.

11:15.912 --> 11:18.480
I don't care about
anything except Brian.

11:18.515 --> 11:21.784
I want Brian.
(sobs)

11:23.587 --> 11:26.488
You want me to put a
dead dog under your tree?

11:26.523 --> 11:28.424
Yes.

11:31.227 --> 11:33.495
(sniffles) And, uh,

11:33.530 --> 11:35.297
I-I'd like
a bike, too.

11:38.960 --> 11:42.929
<i>ANNOUNCER: We now return to The Year
Without a Santa Claus or Sex.</i>

11:42.964 --> 11:44.130
Daddy, where's
Santa Clau...

11:44.165 --> 11:45.265
I don't know, okay?!

11:45.299 --> 11:46.600
Should I ask Mom?

11:46.634 --> 11:50.003
(laughs) I don't know,
she's so busy with her job.

11:50.037 --> 11:52.405
VINNY:
Hello there, Stewart.

11:52.440 --> 11:54.374
What's this?
What are you doing, Vinny?

11:54.408 --> 11:55.942
Vinny? Who's Vinny?

11:55.977 --> 11:59.546
My name is Brian,
aka your favorite dog.

11:59.580 --> 12:01.414
Hey, whose leg do
you gotta gagoosh

12:01.449 --> 12:04.017
to get an Amaretto Di
Saronno around here?

12:04.051 --> 12:05.885
Oh, forget it, Vinny.
You're not Brian.

12:05.920 --> 12:07.821
Come on, I went through
a lot of trouble.

12:07.855 --> 12:10.924
For example, I know Brian
was rather into politics,

12:10.958 --> 12:12.392
so I read the newspaper.

12:12.426 --> 12:15.495
What is goin' on with
all these politics, huh?

12:15.529 --> 12:18.131
Well, that is about Brian's
level of political awareness.

12:18.165 --> 12:19.633
Yeah, and you know
how Brian wrote

12:19.667 --> 12:20.867
<i>Wish It, Want It, Do It?</i>

12:20.901 --> 12:22.335
Well, I wrote
a book, too.

12:22.370 --> 12:23.436
A little
something called

12:23.471 --> 12:24.871
<i>Wish It, Want It,
You Blew It.</i>

12:24.905 --> 12:26.039
Really?

12:26.073 --> 12:28.942
Yup. Let me read
you an expert.

12:28.976 --> 12:30.677
"You wish you
were a millionaire.

12:30.711 --> 12:32.879
"You want more money.
Guess what.

12:32.913 --> 12:34.014
"You blew it.

12:34.048 --> 12:35.782
"You wish you could
change the neighborhood.

12:35.816 --> 12:37.817
"You want to be
a selectman.

12:37.852 --> 12:39.019
"You blew it.

12:39.053 --> 12:40.887
"You wish you could
open up a restaurant.

12:40.921 --> 12:42.889
"You did not want to
pay protection money.

12:42.923 --> 12:44.057
"Knock, knock.
Who's there?

12:44.091 --> 12:45.191
You blew it."

12:45.226 --> 12:46.326
You blew it who?

12:46.360 --> 12:47.460
You blew it bad.

12:47.495 --> 12:49.663
You know what the last
page of the book is?

12:49.697 --> 12:52.198
A mirror. So you can see
exactly who blew it.

12:52.233 --> 12:53.333
Being you.

12:53.367 --> 12:55.168
Look, I appreciate
all this, Vinny,

12:55.202 --> 12:57.404
but there's only one Brian,

12:57.438 --> 13:00.006
and it's tough for me
that he's gone,

13:00.041 --> 13:02.742
especially around the holidays.

13:02.777 --> 13:05.045
Okay, I know what'll
cheer you up.

13:05.079 --> 13:07.514
How about you open up one
of those Christmas presents?

13:07.548 --> 13:08.715
It's from me.

13:08.749 --> 13:10.750
Merry Christmas.

13:10.785 --> 13:13.019
What the hell?
There's a foot in this box.

13:13.054 --> 13:15.121
That was supposed to
go to somebody else.

13:15.156 --> 13:16.456
I'm very sorry.

13:16.490 --> 13:17.724
Well, my friends,

13:17.758 --> 13:20.393
I think Johnny "The Foot"
Giatelli is dead.

13:20.428 --> 13:21.561
Oh no.

13:21.595 --> 13:24.164
They killed Frankie
"Choo-Choo" Chinelli instead.

13:24.198 --> 13:25.532
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
wait a minute.

13:25.566 --> 13:27.233
You sure that's
what this means?

13:27.268 --> 13:29.703
Could be they killed
Davey "The Box" Frateli.

13:29.737 --> 13:30.904
- Ooh. - Ooh.
- Ooh.

13:30.938 --> 13:32.539
Hold on, it
could also be

13:32.573 --> 13:35.041
they killed Jimmy
"Tissue Paper" Scungili.

13:35.076 --> 13:37.877
I just saw Jimmy yesterday
at my kid's christening.

13:37.912 --> 13:39.446
So maybe
it wasn't Jimmy.

13:39.480 --> 13:40.647
Maybe this
means they killed

13:40.681 --> 13:42.449
Anthony "The Air
Around the Box" Minetti.

13:42.483 --> 13:43.817
(gunshot)

13:43.851 --> 13:45.151
Oh, no, they killed

13:45.186 --> 13:47.053
Sal "Holding The Box
That We Can't Figure Out

13:47.088 --> 13:49.222
What The Box Means" Casella.

13:49.256 --> 13:51.324
Here, I got this
for you, too.

13:52.460 --> 13:53.593
A bowling shirt?

13:53.627 --> 13:54.928
You can wear
it anywhere.

13:54.962 --> 13:56.863
To the beach,
a wedding on the beach,

13:56.897 --> 13:59.399
beach graduation,
beach funeral,

13:59.433 --> 14:01.868
business conference
which could be at a beach,

14:01.902 --> 14:03.002
a stroll
through the park,

14:03.037 --> 14:05.171
should that park be
adjacent to a beach.

14:05.206 --> 14:06.339
Thanks.

14:06.374 --> 14:07.807
What, you
don't like it?

14:07.842 --> 14:09.309
How's about we
go to the mall

14:09.343 --> 14:10.844
and pick out something
you do like?

14:10.878 --> 14:13.213
Well, I suppose
I could browse the toy store.

14:13.247 --> 14:15.081
Possibly pick up
a new action figure.

14:15.116 --> 14:16.583
That's the spirit.

14:16.617 --> 14:18.737
All right, I better get out
of these professor clothes

14:18.753 --> 14:20.754
before I kick
my own ass.

14:25.025 --> 14:27.827
Okay, Stewie.
Pick anything you want, on me.

14:27.862 --> 14:30.663
I don't know. I hate the toy
store this close to Christmas.

14:30.698 --> 14:32.265
It's always
been picked clean.

14:32.299 --> 14:33.933
There's plenty of
good stuff here.

14:33.968 --> 14:36.936
Look at this, heavy
bronze sheep bookends.

14:36.971 --> 14:39.372
What kid wouldn't want
to play with these?

14:39.407 --> 14:41.074
"Baa. What are
you lookin' at?"

14:41.108 --> 14:43.143
"Not much, that's
what I'm lookin' at."

14:43.177 --> 14:44.411
"You want to have a go?"

14:44.445 --> 14:45.545
"I'd watch what I say

14:45.579 --> 14:47.614
with that other sheep
right behind you."

14:48.549 --> 14:49.983
I played this as a kid.

14:50.017 --> 14:52.018
Course, I had to do
it with ashtrays,

14:52.052 --> 14:53.653
but I think the
sheep is better.

14:55.489 --> 14:57.290
Wait a minute.
Who is that?

15:02.196 --> 15:04.531
I think... I think
I know that boy.

15:18.746 --> 15:20.780
Vinny,
that stocking cap.

15:20.815 --> 15:21.981
It's mine.

15:23.818 --> 15:25.685
That boy is me.

15:25.719 --> 15:28.221
Of course.
It's me from the past.

15:28.255 --> 15:30.390
Several months ago,
I time-traveled ahead

15:30.424 --> 15:31.925
to purchase
that Christmas toy.

15:31.959 --> 15:34.093
I don't understand, so
I'm angry and hungry.

15:34.128 --> 15:35.929
I'm gonna go
punch a sandwich.

15:37.198 --> 15:39.299
Wow, good timing,
little fella.

15:39.333 --> 15:40.600
This just
came out today.

15:40.634 --> 15:43.336
(chuckling): Yeah, I kind of
knew that already.

15:43.370 --> 15:45.805
The time machine return pad
is in the backpack

15:45.840 --> 15:47.240
that other Stewie is wearing.

15:47.274 --> 15:49.108
I must get
my hands on it, Vinny.

15:49.143 --> 15:50.343
Vinny?

15:50.377 --> 15:52.212
That was a
tough sandwich.

15:52.246 --> 15:53.880
As tough as your
mom's fat face.

15:53.914 --> 15:55.315
Hey, leave my mother
out of this.

15:55.349 --> 15:57.650
That woman stitched gloves
till she was 90.

15:57.685 --> 15:59.686
I heard she was
good with her hands.

15:59.720 --> 16:00.920
Nice.

16:00.955 --> 16:03.423
Hey, everybody, we got
a funny sandwich here.

16:03.457 --> 16:04.691
(bleep) (bleep).

16:04.725 --> 16:06.626
Vinny, I need you
to get that Stewie

16:06.660 --> 16:07.961
to take off
his backpack.

16:07.995 --> 16:09.662
Listen, Stewie,
I'm not following.

16:09.697 --> 16:10.930
I don't have time
to explain.

16:10.965 --> 16:12.131
I've got to
steal something...

16:12.166 --> 16:13.967
That's it. You've
already explained.

16:14.001 --> 16:15.802
You got to steal
something. Got it.

16:15.836 --> 16:17.370
Wait-Wait a sec,
what's your plan?

16:17.404 --> 16:19.239
Trust me, I think
I know you well enough

16:19.273 --> 16:20.940
to know how to distract
the other you.

16:25.346 --> 16:26.946
Hey, how you doing?

16:26.981 --> 16:29.182
This may sound a little
presumptuous of me,

16:29.216 --> 16:31.618
but, uh, you ever
do any modeling?

16:31.652 --> 16:32.852
Well, not
professionally,

16:32.887 --> 16:34.521
but I-I-I have
thought about it.

16:34.555 --> 16:35.722
You ought to.

16:35.756 --> 16:38.191
What are you, like,
six-three? Six-four?

16:38.225 --> 16:40.226
Y-Y-You're in...
you're in the ballpark.

16:40.261 --> 16:41.728
I-I-I carry
myself taller.

16:41.762 --> 16:43.396
Good posture,
very important.

16:43.430 --> 16:44.898
Oh, I agree.

16:44.932 --> 16:46.533
Let me see, let me see.

16:49.003 --> 16:50.036
That's good.

16:50.070 --> 16:51.504
But I feel like that backpack

16:51.539 --> 16:53.306
might be hiding
some figure flaws.

16:53.340 --> 16:57.577
(laughs) Well, that is where
you are wrong, my friend.

17:02.850 --> 17:04.150
You know, my friends ask me,

17:04.184 --> 17:06.586
"Stewie, why do you throw up
after every meal?"

17:06.620 --> 17:07.954
This.

17:07.988 --> 17:09.255
This is why.

17:11.959 --> 17:14.060
All right, whatever
you gotta do, do it quick.

17:14.094 --> 17:15.595
The other you
is in the back

17:15.629 --> 17:17.997
changing into a pair of
tap shoes, for some reason.

17:18.032 --> 17:20.266
OTHER STEWIE: ♪ Animal crackers
in my soup... ♪

17:20.301 --> 17:21.668
Hey, where did
that guy go?

17:21.702 --> 17:24.437
Excellent. Now all I've got
to do is set the coordinates

17:24.471 --> 17:25.972
to the moment before
Brian got killed

17:26.006 --> 17:27.106
and I can save him.

17:27.141 --> 17:29.409
Oh, yeah, Scott Bakula
and all that.

17:29.443 --> 17:31.077
Yes, Vinny.
Scott Bakula.

17:31.111 --> 17:33.346
Well, thank you
for everything.

17:33.380 --> 17:34.547
You bet.

17:34.582 --> 17:37.483
You realize if I save Brian,

17:37.518 --> 17:39.319
my family won't
get another dog,

17:39.353 --> 17:41.821
which means we
will never have met.

17:41.855 --> 17:44.624
I'll probably
never see you again.

17:44.658 --> 17:46.960
Oh.

17:46.994 --> 17:50.229
So, I think this is good-bye.

17:50.264 --> 17:52.565
Hey, I'm man's best friend,

17:52.600 --> 17:55.034
not some stupid baby's
best friend, right?

18:04.244 --> 18:07.113
Good dog, Vinny.
Good dog.

18:07.147 --> 18:09.983
Georgette,
I'm coming home.

18:10.017 --> 18:11.784
Who the hell is Georgette?

18:15.022 --> 18:16.990
Okay, Brian, I'm just
putting this out there,

18:17.024 --> 18:20.159
but I'm a baby and only dicks
don't let babies win.

18:20.194 --> 18:21.761
God, look at
this day, huh?

18:21.795 --> 18:23.796
You know, usually, I'd be
sitting inside writing,

18:23.831 --> 18:25.732
you'd be working on
one of your machines.

18:25.766 --> 18:27.433
But here we are
enjoying it.

18:27.468 --> 18:29.268
Yes, it is a nice
change of pace.

18:29.303 --> 18:31.137
Oh, wait, I gotta
go grab my knee pads.

18:31.171 --> 18:33.906
I was using them for...
for, for this other thing.

18:33.941 --> 18:35.475
Anyway, I-I'll be
right back.

18:42.950 --> 18:44.350
Brian, look out!

18:46.620 --> 18:47.720
What the hell?

18:47.755 --> 18:50.356
You're alive,
my friend.

18:50.391 --> 18:51.424
What?
Course I'm alive.

18:51.458 --> 18:52.692
What the hell's
going on here?

18:52.726 --> 18:54.427
Brian, that car
killed you.

18:54.461 --> 18:57.764
And when it did, a little
part of me died as well.

18:57.798 --> 18:58.998
I couldn't live without you.

18:59.033 --> 19:01.434
So I came back from the future
to save your life.

19:01.468 --> 19:02.835
Whoa. Wait,
wait a minute.

19:02.870 --> 19:04.003
What are you
talking about?

19:04.038 --> 19:05.471
I saw you destroy
your time machine.

19:05.506 --> 19:07.740
Yes, but luckily, I ran into
another me from the past,

19:07.775 --> 19:09.909
so I stole his return pad
and came back here.

19:09.943 --> 19:11.210
Oh, that reminds me.

19:11.245 --> 19:13.246
I've gotta send this back
where it came from.

19:18.352 --> 19:20.086
Hmm. I'm starting to think
that guy

19:20.120 --> 19:21.654
wasn't a real modeling agent.

19:21.689 --> 19:23.423
And I'm starting to think
that other guy

19:23.457 --> 19:25.658
wasn't a real
penis-butt inspector.

19:25.693 --> 19:29.162
Wow, Stewie, thank you
for saving my life.

19:29.196 --> 19:30.930
You know, a whole
lot of other families

19:30.964 --> 19:32.965
would've just gotten a
different dog and moved on.

19:33.000 --> 19:35.168
Oh, oh, we could,
we could never

19:35.202 --> 19:37.203
do something
like that, Brian.

19:37.237 --> 19:39.439
Stewie, what's
happening to you?

19:39.473 --> 19:42.341
I think... My time line
is being erased.

19:42.376 --> 19:45.278
The time line where
you died no longer exists.

19:46.547 --> 19:48.381
Merry Christmas, Brian.

19:49.483 --> 19:51.184
Hey, who were you
talking to out here?

19:51.218 --> 19:54.320
A pretty awesome guy.

19:54.354 --> 19:55.421
Oh, "pretty awesome guy."

19:55.456 --> 19:56.689
Why don't you
marry him, huh?

19:56.724 --> 19:57.724
All right, game on.

19:57.758 --> 19:59.759
Aah!
(imitates crowd cheering)

19:59.793 --> 20:02.729
Stew-S-A.
Stew-S-A. Stew-S-A.

20:08.869 --> 20:12.438
Oven mitts.
Wow, thanks, Mom.

20:12.473 --> 20:13.906
Now you don't
have to ask me

20:13.941 --> 20:16.642
if everything is hot
before you touch it.

20:16.677 --> 20:19.679
Are... are
the oven mitts hot?

20:19.713 --> 20:22.315
Here you go, Stewie.
Merry Christmas.

20:26.887 --> 20:29.822
Brian, it's-it's...
wonderful. Thank you.

20:29.857 --> 20:32.091
Well, you gave me
the greatest gift of all.

20:32.126 --> 20:33.760
I'll tell you
about it sometime.

20:33.794 --> 20:34.927
Brian.

20:34.962 --> 20:36.562
Are we pregnant?

20:36.597 --> 20:38.633
What? No, Stewie,
it's nothing like that.

20:38.634 --> 20:40.167
Okay, well, I
have to tell you,

20:40.202 --> 20:41.302
I'm a little
bit relieved.

20:41.336 --> 20:43.787
Look, just, just, thanks
for everything, Stewie.

20:43.788 --> 20:46.691
You're my best friend
and I love you.

20:46.692 --> 20:48.327
All I can say, Brian,

20:48.352 --> 20:51.092
is you've been making
really creepy eye contact

20:51.093 --> 20:53.789
with me all morning
and I want it to stop right now.

20:53.790 --> 21:54.790
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru